From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:32:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: validate Uke HDR state and send VSC/HDR SDPs

Adapt the packet, color and stream-lifetime portions of Xilin Wu's HDR10 v2
series to the existing 7.2.12 bridge and controller API. Retain the original
KDE compositor and expose real HDR metadata/BT.2020 connector properties only
on the Uke SM7675 DP path. Reject HDR10 without sink support or sufficient
link bandwidth, retain full-range RGB and program the Generic2 HDR SDP.

Balance failed stream power references and PHY ownership, avoid SDP accesses
without link clocks and report link failures asynchronously. Export cached
stream parameters without AUX, MMIO or runtime-resume side effects. This
source change does not qualify HDR, four-lane negotiation, MST or USB fallback
on a physical tablet.

Based on Xilin Wu's GPL-2.0-only MSM DP HDR10 v2 patches 04/05/08-10/13/14/17-20:
https://lore.kernel.org/dri-devel/20261009-msm-dp-hdr10-v2-0-1835d4966da3@radxa.com/

